# Setup instructions

## Option 1: Google Colab development environment

Follow these steps to open a notebook in Colab.

1. Go to [Google Colab](https://colab.research.google.com) and sign in.
2. Choose Upload notebook → GitHub tab.
3. Paste https://github.com/algolab-quantique/qest-hack26 and click the search icon.
4. Click the notebook you want to open.
5. **Important**: Click the "Copy to Drive" button in the toolbar at the top, otherwise your results will not be saved. A new version of the notebook will open in a new tab, and that’s the one you should work in.
6. Uncomment the first cell of the notebook and execute it to install all the Python dependencies in the Colab environment.

## Option 2: Local development environment

Follow these steps if you want to run the notebook locally.

1. Clone the repository https://github.com/algolab-quantique/qest-hack26 on your local drive and open the folder `cd qest-hack26`.
2. Create a Python virtual environment by running `python3 -m venv venv`. The notebook have been tested with Python versions 3.12 and 3.13.
3. Activate your virtual environment `source venv/bin/activate` (Mac/Linux) or `source venv\Scripts\activate` (Windows).
4. Install the Python dependencies `pip install -r requirements.txt`. Leave the first cell commented out, since it’s only needed on Colab.

Happy QEst Hack!
